---
import Tunnel from '../../../layouts/Tunnel.astro';
import Choice from '../../../components/Choice.astro';
// DRAFT
---
<Tunnel title="Backup First | Save My Gig!" status="Quick_Fix">
  <div class="review-flag">DRAFT, review pending.</div>
  <div class="step-label">Step 3</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Safety copy before the rebuild</h2>

  <!-- Said "We're about to format this drive", which is false on the branch the
       DJ is actually sent down: YES here goes to /repair, which does not
       format. The format is two screens further on and only down one route.
       Overstating it here trains people to skim the warning that IS real. -->
  <div class="alert-card" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">
    <div style="font-size:20px" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</div>
    <div>Everything after this point can end in a format. <strong>Copy your music off first.</strong></div>
  </div>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Copy the whole drive to the computer, or at minimum the <strong>Contents</strong> folder.</li>
    <li>If some files fail, copy what you can and note which ones. Skipped files are gone for good if this drive gets formatted later, so if any of them matter, take the fresh-drive route instead and keep this one intact.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="question">Did the copy complete?</p>

  <Choice step="qf_backup"
    a={{ href: '/protocol/quick-fix/repair', label: 'YES, MUSIC IS SAFE' }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/quick-fix/fresh-usb', label: 'NO, COPY KEEPS FAILING', desc: 'The drive is failing. We build tonight on a different one.' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
